# MCP client wiring — generated by install.py with this checkout's absolute path.
# Same reasoning as config.json below: it names the machine it was written on,
# and the client's only symptom is a generic "failed to connect".
.mcp.json
.codex/config.toml

# User config (has API keys)
config.json
/config.json
config*.json
!config.example.json

# The neutral fallback that ships inside the package. Anchored on purpose: an
# unanchored `!config.default.json` would re-include a file of that name at any
# depth, which is how `mutants/config.example.json` once ended up in a build
# (docs/audits/2026-09-16.md, C04). The cost of getting this wrong is silent —
# hatchling applies these rules to the wheel, so an ignored file is a file that
# never embarks, and the symptom is a FileNotFoundError in production only.
!src/academic_hunter/core/infra/config.default.json

# mutmut sandbox — rebuild it with `mutmut run`; 7 MB of copies, not source
mutants/
